# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.js

# testing
/coverage
# Vitest's own scratch root. Browser mode parks attachments here and fills in a
# `failure-screenshots/` tree under it for every failing test; both are
# diagnostics for the run that produced them, so they are worth looking at and
# never worth committing.
# Vitest 5 moved both into this one directory. Vitest 4 wrote attachments to
# `/.vitest-attachments/` and the failure screenshot into a `__screenshots__/`
# beside the test, and those were the two entries this block used to carry -
# the diagnostics no longer land in either place, so both are gone.
# `__screenshots__/` is deliberately not ignored now rather than merely unused:
# in 5 that directory belongs to `toMatchScreenshot`, and what it holds is the
# *reference* image - a baseline meant to be reviewed and committed, like any
# other snapshot. Ignoring it keeps the baseline out of the repository, and
# `toMatchScreenshot` fails on a reference it cannot find, so the visual test
# would fail on CI on every run. Only the `-actual`/`-diff` images a comparison
# failure drops beside the reference are worth an ignore, and that can wait for
# the first test to produce them.
/.vitest/

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# Claude Code working directory (agent worktrees, launch config, local settings).
# Hundreds of MB of scratch checkouts - never wanted in a commit or a Docker
# build context. Two exceptions, both about working on this repo rather than
# about one machine: the signing hook, and the skills. That is also why the
# pattern is `.claude/*` - git cannot re-include a path whose parent directory is
# excluded outright.
# What is NOT re-included is `settings.local.json`, which registers the hook, and
# a `git worktree add` copies nothing untracked - so a `web-N-*` worktree gets the
# script without anything wired to it. See DECISIONS.md, "The skills are repo
# content; what wires up the hook is not".
.claude/*
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/skills/
# Re-including the directory re-includes whatever Python leaves in it. The api
# repo ignores this globally; a JavaScript repo has no reason to, until now.
.claude/hooks/__pycache__/

# Playwright MCP server scratch output (accessibility snapshots, console logs).
.playwright-mcp/

# MapLibre's worker, copied out of node_modules by scripts/copy-maplibre-worker.mjs
# so the renderer boots it from this origin rather than from a `blob:` URL. Build
# output that happens to live under `public/`, not repository content - the copy
# has to match the installed version, and a committed one would go stale the next
# time the dependency moves. `predev`/`prebuild`/`pretest` put it back.
/public/maplibre/

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# local env files
.env*.local
.env

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
